t":"2026-10-07T20:07:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124266","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124266","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124266.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124266.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe [NavigationMesh](https://github.com/ALiwoto/official-godot/blob/e7b12e749220a75ef87e800e080bd2732ad46854/scene/resources/navigation_mesh.h#L37) class itself does not depend on 2D module directly, however, currently it's not being registered in the typesystem due to an `#ifndef`.\r\n\r\nThis PR brings it out of that if macro so it gets registered.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nFor example, imagine you want to create a server for a 3D game, and you don't need to process anything related to 2D space; but you still need the 3D module and navigation processing. with current godot code, your code will crash at startup when trying to load your resources, because godot can't find `NavigationMesh` type.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124266/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124266/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}